ok   set owns its bytes and get returns an independent copy
ok   empty keys and values round-trip
ok   a key of exactly 64 KiB is accepted
ok   huge finite TTLs are capped before multiplication
ok   zero and NaN TTLs are rejected
ok   max_bytes cannot overflow the FFI C long
ok   sweep budgets cannot overflow the FFI C long
ok   excessive index capacities are rejected
ok   sweep zero leaves all counters unchanged
ok   small sweep budgets rotate through every shard
ok   copies observe the same native closed state
ok   every operation reports a closed cache
ok   concurrent operations and repeated close preserve the replacement
ok   statistics snapshots remain separate during concurrent GC
